maluos-branding (0.3.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * /usr/lib/os-release is a symlink to the installed variant's file
    (os-release.server or os-release.desktop), set by apply-variant; adds
    LOGO=maluos-logo.
  * New binary maluos-desktop-branding: VARIANT="Desktop", login screen
    logo and background, MaluOS wallpapers (light and dark), the
    distributor icon, the session entry named MaluOS, and the boot splash
    watermark (plymouth-theme-spinner's links to Ubuntu's logo).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

maluos-branding (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Remove Ubuntu from everything a user sees: os-release ID=maluos
    ID_LIKE="ubuntu debian" with maluos.com URLs, lsb-release,
    /etc/legal, motd extras off, Pro client hooks diverted and timers
    masked, GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR MaluOS, explicit unattended-upgrades
    origins.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:38:01 +0000

